peace treaty</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Both occurred after 1945</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>WH_U05_L06_Q04 F04 Ghetto Einsatzgruppen</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> WH_U05_L06_Q04</p>Which distinction is correct?]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review Unit 5 Lesson 6 evidence and reasoning.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>ABCD</answernumbering><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Ghettos forcibly confined Jews; Einsatzgruppen carried out mass shootings, especially in occupied Eastern Europe</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Ghettos were killing centers built only in Germany; Einsatzgruppen were rescuers</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Both were resistance organizations</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Neither involved Nazi policy</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>WH_U05_L06_Q05 F05 Killing center</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> WH_U05_L06_Q05</p>A <strong>killing center</strong> was created primarily for]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review Unit 5 Lesson 6 evidence and reasoning.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>ABCD</answernumbering><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>systematic mass murder</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>competitive elections</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>refugee resettlement</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>military training</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>WH_U05_L06_Q06 V01 Timeline</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> WH_U05_L06_Q06</p><table border="1" cellpadding="6" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><caption><strong>Escalation of Nazi persecution and mass murder</strong></caption><tr style="background:#fee2e2"><th>Date</th><th>Development</th></tr><tr><td>1933</td><td>Early exclusion, arrests, boycotts, and persecution</td></tr><tr><td>1935</td><td>Nuremberg Laws institutionalize racial exclusion</td></tr><tr><td>Nov. 1938</td><td>Kristallnacht: coordinated anti-Jewish violence</td></tr><tr><td>1939–40</td><td>Occupation and forced confinement in ghettos</td></tr><tr><td>1941</td><td>Einsatzgruppen mass shootings expand after invasion of Soviet Union</td></tr><tr><td>1942</td><td>Deportations and killing-center operations expand</td></tr><tr><td>1943</td><td>Warsaw Ghetto Uprising and other resistance</td></tr><tr><td>1944–45</td><td>Continued deportations; camps liberated as Nazi Germany collapses</td></tr></table><p>Which sequence is accurate?</p>]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review Unit 5 Lesson 6 evidence and reasoning.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>ABCD</answernumbering><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Legal exclusion preceded ghettos, mass shootings, and expanded deportation to killing centers</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Killing centers preceded the 1935 laws</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Liberation preceded Kristallnacht</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The Warsaw Ghetto Uprising occurred in 1933</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>WH_U05_L06_Q07 V02 Timeline escalation</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> WH_U05_L06_Q07</p><table border="1" cellpadding="6" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><caption><strong>Escalation of Nazi persecution and mass murder</strong></caption><tr style="background:#fee2e2"><th>Date</th><th>Development</th></tr><tr><td>1933</td><td>Early exclusion, arrests, boycotts, and persecution</td></tr><tr><td>1935</td><td>Nuremberg Laws institutionalize racial exclusion</td></tr><tr><td>Nov. 1938</td><td>Kristallnacht: coordinated anti-Jewish violence</td></tr><tr><td>1939–40</td><td>Occupation and forced confinement in ghettos</td></tr><tr><td>1941</td><td>Einsatzgruppen mass shootings expand after invasion of Soviet Union</td></tr><tr><td>1942</td><td>Deportations and killing-center operations expand</td></tr><tr><td>1943</td><td>Warsaw Ghetto Uprising and other resistance</td></tr><tr><td>1944–45</td><td>Continued deportations; camps liberated as Nazi Germany collapses</td></tr></table><p>What does the timeline demonstrate?</p>]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review Unit 5 Lesson 6 evidence and reasoning.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>ABCD</answernumbering><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Persecution escalated through changing policies, war, institutions, and decisions over time</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Mass murder began in one identical form in 1933</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>No resistance occurred</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Laws became less discriminatory each year</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>WH_U05_L06_Q08 V03 Map</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> WH_U05_L06_Q08</p><div style="border:3px solid #374151;background:#f3f4f6;padding:10px"><h3>Schematic map: Nazi-controlled Europe and persecution sites</h3><svg viewBox="0 0 760 290" style="width:100%;background:#e5e7eb" role="img" aria-label="Simplified map showing Nazi Germany, occupied Europe, ghettos in occupied Poland, and major killing centers"><rect x="80" y="55" width="210" height="160" fill="#fecaca"/><text x="120" y="135">Occupied Western Europe</text><rect x="300" y="55" width="125" height="150" fill="#f87171"/><text x="320" y="120">Nazi</text><text x="315" y="142">Germany</text><rect x="435" y="50" width="150" height="180" fill="#fde68a"/><text x="460" y="85">Occupied Poland</text><circle cx="485" cy="120" r="7" fill="#1d4ed8"/><text x="497" y="125">major ghettos</text><polygon points="485,160 493,177 477,177" fill="#111827"/><text x="500" y="176">Treblinka</text><polygon points="535,195 543,212 527,212" fill="#111827"/><text x="550" y="210">Auschwitz-Birkenau</text><rect x="600" y="45" width="120" height="190" fill="#c4b5fd"/><text x="620" y="135">Occupied</text><text x="610" y="157">Soviet lands</text></svg><p><b>Legend:</b> red = Nazi Germany/occupied areas; blue circle = ghetto region; black triangle = killing center. <small>Schematic—not complete and not boundary precise.</small></p></div><p>Which geographic relationship is shown?</p>]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review Unit 5 Lesson 6 evidence and reasoning.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>ABCD</answernumbering><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Major ghettos and killing centers were concentrated in occupied Poland, while Nazi control extended across Europe</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>All killing centers were in Britain</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Occupied Soviet lands lay west of France</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Germany controlled no neighboring territory</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>WH_U05_L06_Q09 V04 Map limitation</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> WH_U05_L06_Q09</p><div style="border:3px solid #374151;background:#f3f4f6;padding:10px"><h3>Schematic map: Nazi-controlled Europe and persecution sites</h3><svg viewBox="0 0 760 290" style="width:100%;background:#e5e7eb" role="img" aria-label="Simplified map showing Nazi Germany, occupied Europe, ghettos in occupied Poland, and major killing centers"><rect x="80" y="55" width="210" height="160" fill="#fecaca"/><text x="120" y="135">Occupied Western Europe</text><rect x="300" y="55" width="125" height="150" fill="#f87171"/><text x="320" y="120">Nazi</text><text x="315" y="142">Germany</text><rect x="435" y="50" width="150" height="180" fill="#fde68a"/><text x="460" y="85">Occupied Poland</text><circle cx="485" cy="120" r="7" fill="#1d4ed8"/><text x="497" y="125">major ghettos</text><polygon points="485,160 493,177 477,177" fill="#111827"/><text x="500" y="176">Treblinka</text><polygon points="535,195 543,212 527,212" fill="#111827"/><text x="550" y="210">Auschwitz-Birkenau</text><rect x="600" y="45" width="120" height="190" fill="#c4b5fd"/><text x="620" y="135">Occupied</text><text x="610" y="157">Soviet lands</text></svg><p><b>Legend:</b> red = Nazi Germany/occupied areas; blue circle = ghetto region; black triangle = killing center. <small>Schematic—not complete and not boundary precise.</small></p></div><p>What is an important limitation?</p>]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review Unit 5 Lesson 6 evidence and reasoning.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>ABCD</answernumbering><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>It is simplified and omits many sites, routes, borders, victims, and local experiences</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>It accurately shows every camp</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>It proves geography caused genocide automatically</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>It is a survivor diary</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>WH_U05_L06_Q10 V05 Escalation model</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> WH_U05_L06_Q10</p><div style="border:3px solid #7f1d1d;background:#fff1f2;padding:10px;text-align:center"><h3>Persecution escalation model</h3><p><b>Antisemitic ideology and prejudice</b> → propaganda → legal exclusion → economic/social persecution → forced concentration and deportation → mass murder</p><p style="background:#fef3c7;padding:7px"><b>This sequence was produced through human decisions, institutions, and wartime escalation; it was not inevitable.</b></p></div><p>Why is legal exclusion a significant stage?</p>]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review Unit 5 Lesson 6 evidence and reasoning.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>ABCD</answernumbering><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>State law converted racist ideology into enforceable loss of rights and wider persecution</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>It restored citizenship</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>It ended propaganda</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>It made later decisions inevitable without human action</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>WH_U05_L06_Q11 V06 Camp distinction</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> WH_U05_L06_Q11</p><table border="1" cellpadding="6" style="border-collapse:collapse;width:100%"><caption><strong>Camp-system distinctions</strong></caption><tr style="background:#dbeafe"><th>Type</th><th>Primary function</th><th>Example</th></tr><tr><td>Concentration camp</td><td>Imprisonment, terror, forced labor</td><td>Dachau</td></tr><tr><td>Forced-labor camp</td><td>Exploitation through coerced labor</td><td>Many sites across occupied Europe</td></tr><tr><td>Killing center</td><td>Systematic mass murder</td><td>Treblinka</td></tr><tr><td>Mixed complex</td><td>Multiple functions, including forced labor and mass murder</td><td>Auschwitz-Birkenau</td></tr></table><p>Which statement is accurate?</p>]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review Unit 5 Lesson 6 evidence and reasoning.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>ABCD</answernumbering><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Auschwitz-Birkenau had multiple functions, while Treblinka was created primarily for mass murder</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Dachau was created only as a killing center</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Every camp had an identical primary function</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Forced labor and mass murder were unrelated to Nazi policy</p>]]></text><feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review the evidence.</p>]]></text></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>WH_U05_L06_Q12 V07 Nazi law</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> WH_U05_L06_Q12</p><blockquote style="border-left:5px solid #991b1b;padding:9px;background:#fff1f2"><p>“A citizen of the Reich is only that subject who is of German or kindred blood...”</p><footer>Reich Citizenship Law, September 15, 1935; translated excerpt in the USHMM document collection.</footer></blockquote><p>What does the excerpt directly reveal?</p>]]></text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Review Unit 5 Lesson 6 evidence and reasoning.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>ABCD</answernumbering><answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Citizenship was defined through 